.TH SDL_max 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_max \- Return the greater of two values.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_max(x, y) (((x) > (y)) ? (x) : (y))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a helper macro that might be more clear than writing out the comparisons directly, and works with any type that can be compared with the
.BR >
operator\[char46] However, it double-evaluates both its parameters, so do not use expressions with side-effects here\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I x
the first value to compare\[char46]
.TP
.I y
the second value to compare\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the greater of
.BR x
and
.BR y \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

